WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.680
Hello everybody, my name is Markiplier

00:00:01.680 --> 00:00:05.340
And I'm here to ask you if you kept your promise

00:00:05.720 --> 00:00:08.040
And you may be wondering what promise I'm talking about

00:00:08.040 --> 00:00:12.860
But oddly enough in the beginning of May, I'm talking about your New Years Resolution

00:00:13.080 --> 00:00:15.500
Because I can tell you, if you're starting to get panicked and you're like

00:00:15.500 --> 00:00:16.600
"Oh god I didn't do it!"

00:00:16.600 --> 00:00:21.620
Well don't worry because I'm here to confess that I, myself, fell off the wagon

00:00:21.620 --> 00:00:25.080
If you didn't know, my original goals were to be in the best shape of my life,

00:00:25.080 --> 00:00:27.560
to learn guitar and to learn German

00:00:27.900 --> 00:00:31.720
The fitness goal, like maybe it was vanity that I wanted to do it

00:00:31.720 --> 00:00:33.720
I noticed I was getting a little bit of a belly

00:00:33.720 --> 00:00:38.200
And I wanted to just be in general shape which is a cliche for New Year's resolutions

00:00:38.400 --> 00:00:42.780
Guitar was just because I played trumpet in highschool

00:00:42.780 --> 00:00:47.180
And I know all the stuff about music and I wanted to get back into music and I've always wanted to play guitar

00:00:47.840 --> 00:00:51.220
So I wanted to do that just to get caught up in that world again

00:00:51.220 --> 00:00:55.360
And then language, German, is because my last name is Fischbach

00:00:55.360 --> 00:00:58.380
And that's a very German last name and I thought it would be appropriate

00:00:58.780 --> 00:01:02.800
to actually know the language instead of having people constantly ask me if I speak German

00:01:02.800 --> 00:01:04.980
and telling them "No"

00:01:05.480 --> 00:01:10.000
And unfortunately I have failed in all aspects of those things

00:01:10.000 --> 00:01:12.780
And I know the year's not over yet but in the middle of May

00:01:12.780 --> 00:01:16.800
I thought I would be at least somewhere close to my goals

00:01:18.160 --> 00:01:21.380
And I started to realise why I was failing

00:01:21.380 --> 00:01:23.220
And I could make whatever excuse I wanted

00:01:23.220 --> 00:01:27.440
I could make the excuse of I didn't have the time or I got distracted or things got in the way

00:01:27.720 --> 00:01:32.180
But generally speaking, I realised that I failed in my goals

00:01:32.180 --> 00:01:36.620
because I didn't think of the long term aspects of what I was trying to do

00:01:38.040 --> 00:01:44.400
Because for fitness, I wanted to be in the best shape of my life just because I had vain reasons in mind

00:01:44.400 --> 00:01:48.880
And that's good in by itself, but in terms of being in shape

00:01:48.880 --> 00:01:53.060
that's not really an end goal-type thing because if you work to be in shape

00:01:53.100 --> 00:01:56.220
and then you get to be in shape and then you stop,

00:01:56.660 --> 00:02:00.940
like there was no point in you doing it in the first place, you're just gonna get back out of shape again

00:02:00.960 --> 00:02:02.900
That's a life-long thing

00:02:03.440 --> 00:02:05.760
You need the proper motivation behind it

00:02:06.280 --> 00:02:10.160
And I started to realise after I had a little bit of a health scare again

00:02:10.260 --> 00:02:13.000
Nothing is wrong, I'm totally fine

00:02:13.600 --> 00:02:19.060
But I live in this state where I have to get routine check-ups to make sure my tumour that I had

00:02:19.060 --> 00:02:24.460
before I started YouTube, I have to get checked to make sure it doesn't come back again

00:02:25.220 --> 00:02:31.140
And when I was getting my check-up, there was something they found and I had to get it

00:02:31.140 --> 00:02:34.880
checked more thoroughly, just to spare you the grizzly details

00:02:34.880 --> 00:02:37.480
But it turned out to be fine, there's nothing

00:02:38.260 --> 00:02:41.260
But that's something I have to be mindful of

00:02:41.640 --> 00:02:47.080
So when I originally went after my goal of getting into shape just because I wanted to look good,

00:02:47.240 --> 00:02:51.000
I failed to realise that I wanted to live healthier

00:02:51.600 --> 00:02:55.340
Because I never know if the tumour that I had is going to come back

00:02:56.000 --> 00:03:00.820
And I can increase my odds by exercising and eating better

00:03:00.820 --> 00:03:05.360
and hopefully it'll never come back, but you never know with these things

00:03:05.360 --> 00:03:08.420
And with fitness like, it's a lifelong goal

00:03:09.840 --> 00:03:16.160
And with language and music, I think I was misguided in what I wanted because I didn't have an end goal in mind

00:03:16.200 --> 00:03:19.800
I didn't have something that I really wanted to do with those talents

00:03:20.080 --> 00:03:24.400
I didn't have something like, I didn't know if I wanted to perform with guitar or some reason

00:03:24.400 --> 00:03:27.300
that I was trying to impress someone with guitar

00:03:27.300 --> 00:03:30.540
And with language, I didn't really have an end goal for speaking German

00:03:30.540 --> 00:03:33.280
other than it would have been cool to be able to do that

00:03:34.400 --> 00:03:40.380
But as far as the language goes, I recently actually realised something that was very very important to me

00:03:43.240 --> 00:03:45.840
I talk about my family in Korea a lot

00:03:45.960 --> 00:03:48.440
I talk about them like, undendingly

00:03:48.540 --> 00:03:50.800
I have a lot of family in Korea

00:03:50.840 --> 00:03:55.060
I have numerous aunts and uncles, I have actually 7 aunts

00:03:55.060 --> 00:04:01.500
and I have numerous cousins and a lot of them are very proud of what I've managed to accomplish on YouTube

00:04:01.500 --> 00:04:09.800
and especially my grandma who I love to death but recently, my grandma had a stroke

00:04:10.740 --> 00:04:15.480
and she's doing okay now but this is actually her second stroke

00:04:17.900 --> 00:04:24.760
And to be perfectly honest and to put it bluntly, I don't know how much longer she's going to be okay

00:04:25.760 --> 00:04:26.400
You know?

00:04:27.840 --> 00:04:35.100
Like, it's grim to think about and I hope she lives for quite a bit longer but she's getting older

00:04:35.140 --> 00:04:37.840
and this is her second stroke

00:04:38.960 --> 00:04:43.560
and the first one that she had left her a little bit disabled

00:04:43.980 --> 00:04:49.720
and I have all this family that I talk about all the time and I love very dearly

00:04:50.320 --> 00:04:52.280
but I've never talked to them

00:04:54.380 --> 00:04:56.940
And that's a weird thing to say, it's a weird thing to admit

00:04:56.940 --> 00:05:01.660
I have all this family, this huge supportive family that is so proud of what I've done

00:05:01.660 --> 00:05:08.100
and that loves me and my mom is associated with that, she's here in America but they're all over in Korea

00:05:09.220 --> 00:05:12.260
and maybe two or three of them speak English

00:05:13.620 --> 00:05:15.780
The rest of them just speak Korean

00:05:15.780 --> 00:05:21.360
and some of them speak Japanese but not many of them speak fluent English to carry a conversation

00:05:21.380 --> 00:05:27.940
And it dawned on my that my grandma that I love very dearly, I've never had a conversation with her

00:05:28.580 --> 00:05:34.100
Like I've never really had the chance to talk to her and discover like, her life and where she's come from

00:05:34.100 --> 00:05:39.500
and the struggles that she had when she came down from North Korea right before the war

00:05:39.500 --> 00:05:44.380
and the border went down and my grandpa, who has passed on, and my grandma,

00:05:44.380 --> 00:05:47.760
they abandoned everything they had, they had lands, they had money,

00:05:47.760 --> 00:05:54.420
but it was all going to get taken away from them so they just picked up, left their entire family and ran down South

00:05:55.140 --> 00:05:58.580
And right now they live outside of Seoul and a lot of you guys are scared

00:05:58.580 --> 00:06:01.820
because the situation in Korea seems to be dire but...

00:06:02.620 --> 00:06:08.180
my family is down in South Korea right now and I don't know how to talk to them

00:06:08.720 --> 00:06:09.600
You know...?

00:06:10.080 --> 00:06:16.220
So with that in mind, that is now my reason why I want to learn Korean

00:06:17.340 --> 00:06:22.980
And combined, I started to realise that if I take away the things that I want for just pure vanity

00:06:22.980 --> 00:06:30.080
and have an end in mind for, and I take on the things that I want to do as lifelong challenges

00:06:30.080 --> 00:06:34.040
and lifelong beneficial skills that I will have because

00:06:34.040 --> 00:06:40.200
Number one: I will live healthier and hopefully live longer enough to do the things that I want to do

00:06:40.920 --> 00:06:45.820
And number two: Learn Korean to be able to speak with my family who supports me and loves me

00:06:45.820 --> 00:06:51.880
and hopefully I'll be able to visit Korea again because some of you may not know, I'm half Korean

00:06:52.240 --> 00:06:56.220
I don't know if anyone actually, like there are always some people that are shocked to discover

00:06:56.220 --> 00:06:58.600
that I'm half Korean but yes, I'm half Korean

00:06:59.240 --> 00:07:00.520
and I'm half German

00:07:01.200 --> 00:07:03.760
And I want to be able to talk to my family

00:07:04.540 --> 00:07:07.740
And I want to be able to talk to my grandma, you know?

00:07:08.300 --> 00:07:13.685
And I want to be able to help my mom who is bilingual, she speaks perfectly fluent English

00:07:13.685 --> 00:07:15.300
and perfectly fluent Korean

00:07:15.400 --> 00:07:18.880
And I want to help her because she's starting to forget a little bit of the Korean because she doesn't have

00:07:18.880 --> 00:07:20.480
anyone to talk to in Korean

00:07:20.760 --> 00:07:23.460
And I want my brother to be able to do the same thing

00:07:24.880 --> 00:07:29.920
So these are the reasons why I've kind of refocused what I've wanted

00:07:29.920 --> 00:07:36.500
And if I had to wrap this up in a message for you guys, I wanted to tell you that it's okay to fall off the wagon

00:07:36.660 --> 00:07:42.100
so long as you pick yourself back up and reevaluate why you fell off

00:07:42.860 --> 00:07:44.760
and then refocus and hop back on

00:07:45.200 --> 00:07:52.720
Because it's like, it's hard to just constantly get back up and not change anything of your approach to it

00:07:52.740 --> 00:08:01.880
But in this year and what I've wanted to do, I've realised it's so easy to stop when you think there's an end in mind

00:08:02.700 --> 00:08:05.800
And that applies to anything outside of this, like what I do here on YouTube

00:08:05.800 --> 00:08:11.780
If I thought there was an end, like I wouldn't keep pushing forward and keep hitting it everyday

00:08:11.780 --> 00:08:15.840
because I wouldn't want there to be an end and I would think about that all the time and I would think of

00:08:15.840 --> 00:08:18.940
"Oh when am I gonna stop this thing? When am I gonna stop?"

00:08:18.940 --> 00:08:23.380
It's like, this and what I do on the internet, and what I do in terms of creation,

00:08:23.380 --> 00:08:27.560
and it may not always be YouTube videos but what I do in terms of creation and giving

00:08:27.560 --> 00:08:33.280
Doing the charity streams, I do it because it's a lifelong venture for me

00:08:33.760 --> 00:08:38.340
And I may have an audience or I may not not have an audience or like,

00:08:38.340 --> 00:08:43.260
I may be speaking to an audience of 10 people, I may be speaking to an audience of a million people

00:08:44.500 --> 00:08:52.460
Like, it doesn't matter because for me, that creation is a lifelong journey of self-discovery and learning

00:08:52.460 --> 00:08:57.860
and going forward and trying new things, always always trying new things

00:08:57.860 --> 00:09:04.000
and exploring new territory and that is so fun and I'm just, you know, I'm always grateful

00:09:04.000 --> 00:09:08.020
that you guys are here along for the ride for as long as you want to be here

00:09:08.700 --> 00:09:14.720
But my advice to you is look for the things that really really mean something to you

00:09:15.300 --> 00:09:20.320
and use those as fuel to carry you on to your goals

00:09:20.640 --> 00:09:26.080
And that right there is going to change everything because I can guarantee you

00:09:26.240 --> 00:09:29.840
now that I've focused in on what I really want and what matters to me

00:09:29.960 --> 00:09:37.300
And I can still do guitar as a hobby but I don't, until I find some reason to, to really really really pursue it

00:09:38.580 --> 00:09:44.860
Like until I find the reason, I'm going to shelve that and I'm going to focus on fitness for my own sake

00:09:44.900 --> 00:09:47.700
and in language for my family's sake

00:09:48.820 --> 00:09:50.880
And that really does mean something to me

00:09:52.200 --> 00:09:55.940
So anyway, I just wanted to share that with you guys, I hope you guys are having a wonderful Monday

00:09:55.940 --> 00:10:01.660
I've got a lot of cool stuff, I really am thrilled as the response you guys had to Markipler TV

00:10:01.660 --> 00:10:05.760
We worked really hard on that one and I'm just tickled to death that you guys loved it

00:10:05.760 --> 00:10:11.180
And you can expect a lot more from the characters that you saw in that video

00:10:11.180 --> 00:10:14.280
because we put them in the same room for a reason

00:10:15.380 --> 00:10:19.460
And I think you guys are discovering it very soon and you will see it in the future

00:10:19.460 --> 00:10:21.660
So thank you everybody so much for watching

00:10:21.740 --> 00:10:23.480
Let me know what you think down in the comments below

00:10:23.780 --> 00:10:28.040
And as always, I will see you in the next video

00:10:28.480 --> 00:10:30.000
Buh bye! &lt;3

